{% section %}
# My name has changed!

{% meta post=$post /%}

As of March 2026, I now go by the name **"Paperbark"** online, where previously
I was known as **"Quasar"** or **"QuasarHusky"**. This means
that a lot of my usernames either will be or have already been changed, and my overall
presence online will be quite different from how it used to be.

Be sure to check my [socials page](/socials) for an up-to-date list of where I'm
active, as this will be the first place I update when things change.
{% /section %}

{% section %}
## Who is Paperbark?

![Paperbark in Pony Town standing in the snow beside a pond](./cover.png)

Paperbark is my [ponysona](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ponysona)!

They're a selectively mute unicorn who collects memories into scrapbooks so they can be
preserved for the future. They're a gentle and affectionate pony with a close-knit group
of friends who mostly works in the background archiving things for others to revisit.

They were also named after the [Broad-leaved Paperbark](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melaleuca_quinquenervia) tree, which has a bark colour similar to that of their fur!

{% button href="https://toyhou.se/39037018.paperbark" %}
Read more about Paperbark
{% /button %}
{% /section %}

{% note %}
Note that Paperbark as my OC and Paperbark as "me" are **two distinct things**.
As an OC, they have a different personality and character than my actual irl self and
use different pronouns.

I personally prefer to use **he/him** pronouns, but when talking about the OC you
should use **they/them** pronouns.

Don't worry if this is confusing or if you make a mistake, I totally understand! If in
doubt, don't be afraid to ask.
{% /note %}

{% section %}
## Why the change?

I've used the name "Quasar" since around 2016 as it was the name of my
[fursona](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fursona)
at the time, and considering how major the furry fandom was in my life it made sense to do that.

A lot has changed since then though - I'm involved with more than just the furry fandom
now and I've grown a lot as a person over the last decade, so using my fursona (which
hadn't changed since I first made him) to represent me didn't feel right anymore.

Paperbark came about during 2024 as I was rediscovering My Little Pony and finding my
place within the brony community. They hold a lot of importance to me now and are a symbol
of what I've grown to become, and I feel a stronger connection to them than I ever did to
Quasar.

In a way, this change has been a huge step in understanding my true self and being proud
of who I am and the things I enjoy.
{% /section %}

{% section %}
## What about nicknames?

I'll admit, **"Paperbark"** can be a bit of a mouthful to say, so you can always
just call me **"Paper"** if that's easier.

Or if you really feel like it, ["Peanut Butter"](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1cB3hnkKSYY).
{% /section %}
